[[Open This|DevSecOps]]

---

Key Principles of DevSecOps

* ''Shared Responsibility'': Security is no longer solely the security team's job; it is shared among developers, operations, and security specialists.
* ''Shift Left'': Security testing and considerations begin at the start of the [[SDLC]] (planning/coding) rather than at the end.
* Automation: Automated testing ([[SAST]], [[DAST]], dependency scanning) is embedded into the [[CI/CD]] pipeline to identify flaws early.Culture of Collaboration: Encourages communication between teams to foster faster, more resilient development.

https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/devops/what-is-devsecops#:~:text=DevSecOps%20stands%20for%20development%2C%20security,infrastructure%20security%20from%20the%20start.

Key Stages of the DevSecOps Lifecycle

# Plan: Define security requirements and risk assessment.
# Code: Use secure coding standards and static security testing (SAST).
# Build: Automated scanning for vulnerabilities in dependencies and code.
# Test: Dynamic security testing (DAST) on the running application.
# Deploy: Automated compliance checks before production deployment.
# Operate & Monitor: Continuous monitoring for threats in production and gathering feedback.

https://www.dynatrace.com/news/blog/what-is-devsecops/#:~:text=Automated%20Security%20Testing:,to%20promptly%20address%20critical%20issues.

Key Roles in DevSecOps

# Developers: Write secure code and run initial tests.
# Security Engineers: Define security policies and automate them within the pipeline.
# Operations (Ops): Manage infrastructure, monitoring, and compliance.